# Frontend (`apps/web`)

Extends the core rule and `AGENTS.md`.

- Next.js 16 App Router: async `params` typed with generated `PageProps`; version docs in
  `apps/web/node_modules/next/dist/docs/`.
- Server Components by default; `"use client"` only for state, effects, handlers, browser APIs.
- `src/app/` routes, `src/components/` (`ui/` = shadcn/ui-compatible primitives), `src/hooks/`,
  `src/providers/`, `src/api/` and `src/lib/` (feature logic), `src/utils/` (generic).
  Dependencies point components → hooks → providers → api/lib → utils. Navigation:
  `src/lib/navigation/navigation.ts`.
- Call the API through `src/api/` with `import type` from `@orbit/contracts`.
- No `any`, unsafe `as`, or unexplained suppressions; explicit types on exported APIs.
- Loading, error, empty, and success states for data views. Accessible: semantic HTML, labels,
  keyboard, `focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-ring`.
- Tailwind with `src/styles/` tokens (colors in `tokens.css`); `cn()` from
  `src/utils/common/common.ts`.
- Only `NEXT_PUBLIC_*` reaches the browser; validate in `src/lib/env/env.ts`.
- Verify (AGENTS.md "Verification scope"): small: related tests, lint on changed files,
  `pnpm --filter @orbit/web typecheck`; large: add `pnpm test:web` and `pnpm build`.
